## Why This Is Asked

Assess system design capabilities for regulated, privacy-sensitive AI copilots in multi-tenant SaaS environments, focusing on data governance, residency requirements, and auditable prompt management.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant data compartments and role-based access control
- Versioned knowledge base stored in Azure Blob Storage and grounded via Cognitive Search
- PII redaction using Text Analytics with policy-based gating mechanisms
- Comprehensive audit trails stored in Data Lake Storage, tamper-evident logging, and Event Hubs for governance events
- Canary deployment strategy behind API Management for controlled rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: Durable Function orchestrates KB grounding and compliance checks
const orchestrator = function* (context) {
  const tenantId = context.bindingData.tenantId;
  const query = context.bindingData.query;

  // Redact PII before processing
  const redactedQuery = await redactPII(query);

  // Ground against versioned KB
  const grounding = await searchKB(redactedQuery, tenantId);

  // Generate compliant response
  const response = await generateResponse(grounding);

  // Audit all interactions
  await auditInteraction(tenantId, query, response);

  return response;
};
```

